# Rocketship tokens and themes

Reasons: `_planning/component-review-decisions.md` (decisions 6, 7, 55).

## Where tokens live

- Token values live in `packages/base/src/tokens/` as W3C DTCG 2025.10 files:
  - `foundation.tokens.json`: values shared by light and dark (type, spacing, radii, borders, durations).
  - `light.tokens.json` and `dark.tokens.json`: colours and shadows, the same names in both.
  - `rocketship.resolver.json`: the `mode` modifier that picks light or dark.
- Names are nested groups joined with `-`: `color` → `danger` → `bg` is `--rs-color-danger-bg`. A name that is also a group uses `$root`: `color.accent.$root`.
- An alias is a reference: `"$value": "{space.4}"`. It is the same in light and dark.
- Only colours and shadows may differ between modes.

## Changing tokens

- Adding, renaming or removing a token needs Shane's approval.
- Edit the JSON, then run `pnpm --filter @labcat2020/rocketship tokens`. It regenerates `styles/mixins/token-map.scss`.
- Never edit `token-map.scss` or the token part of `variables.scss` by hand.
- In the same change, update the Foundations story for the token: `apps/astro/src/stories/components/ColorsDocument.astro`, `SpacingDocument.astro`, `BordersDocument.astro` or `ShadowsDocument.astro`, aliases included.
- `variables.scss` holds only custom properties on `:root` and inside `@media`. No class selectors. It is the only Sass file that may `@use` a file inside `styles/mixins/` directly.

## Light and dark

- Modes follow `color-scheme`. `:root` sets `color-scheme: light dark`, so the OS preference applies.
- Colour pairs compile to `light-dark()`. Shadow pairs compile to layered shadows whose inactive layer is transparent, so each mode keeps its exact shape.
- A theme picker forces a mode by setting `color-scheme` on `:root` or any subtree.
- Variable names are the same in both modes; only values change.

## Standalone components

- Components work without Rocketship's styles: every `rs-token()` carries its light and dark default as a fallback.
- A standalone consumer only needs `:root { color-scheme: light dark; }` for dark mode.

## Themes

- Rocketship ("space-station") is the default theme. It lives in `packages/base` and must look good and pass accessibility on its own.
- Each of the eight planet themes (Earth, Mars, …) is a complete theme with its own light and dark, never a layer on top of Rocketship.
- A planet theme is its own package with the same layout: `packages/theme-<planet>/src/tokens/`. It contains tokens only, no components, and uses the same token names.
- Theming is CSS variables only; the base experience needs no JavaScript.
- Consumers can use the default theme with no setup, swap in a planet theme by including its CSS, and override any `--rs-*` variable in their own project.
